      "side": 1,
      "message": "On a QUIC client, initial_max_streams_bidi caps streams the peer may open, and HTTP/3 servers never open bidirectional streams — so this value does not bound concurrent requests the way the name suggests; the server\u0027s own initial_max_streams_bidi does. Advertising it is harmless, but could the javadoc say what it actually limits so nobody tunes it expecting more in-flight requests?",
      "revId": "44ee90a510f3386139d634871be5224f21275475",
      "serverId": "7fc14799-209e-464c-9743-7a06c2c21a81"
    },
